        "data_description": {
          "scan_interval_minutes": "How often to refresh live snapshot values — instantaneous power, voltage, frequency, SoC. Lower is fresher but uses more API calls. The Growatt cloud refreshes ~once per minute upstream, so values below 1 don't help. Range 1–60.",
          "slow_scan_interval_minutes": "How often to refresh slow-changing data — kWh totals, settings, chart aggregates. Cached between refreshes and served at the live cadence. Default 5 matches the per-endpoint rate-limit window. Range 1–60.",
          "sph_data_source": "Standard uses sph_system_status (the original endpoint). Detailed uses sph_all_params, which adds per-string PV currents, battery and inverter temperatures, backup output, and load voltage; it also returns grid-import totals so the chart endpoint isn't called. Pick Detailed if you want the extra sensors."
        }
      }
    },
